[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3622824)[0m **Step 1: Understand the graph and reachability**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3622824)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3622824)[0m - The graph has two edges: `B->D` and `C->A`.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3622824)[0m - We define reachability as follows: A node is reachable from another if there is a path of edges from the former to the latter.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3622824)[0m - Node values are determined as:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3622824)[0m   - A node is 1 if it is a downstream descendant of the perturbed node.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3622824)[0m   - A node is 0 otherwise.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3622824)[0m   - The perturbed node is always 0.
