[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m **Step 1: Understanding the candidate graph**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m The candidate graph is **A -> B**. This means:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - A is a direct upstream cause of B.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - A does not have any other edges.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - B is the only downstream node reachable from A.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
