[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - C is perturbed, so C is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - B is a downstream descendant of C? No. C has no outgoing edges in the candidate graph (only A -> B), so B is not a descendant of C.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - So B is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - C is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - D is not a descendant of C, so D is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m Expected output: **C:0, B:0, D:0**  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m Observed output: **C:0, B:1, D:0**  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m This is **inconsistent** because B is not a descendant of C.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m **Perturb(D)**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - D is perturbed, so D is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - B is a downstream descendant of D? No, D has no outgoing edges.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - So B is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - C is not a descendant of D.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - D is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m Expected output: **D:0, B:0, C:0**  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m Observed output: **D:0, B:0, C:0**  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m This is **consistent**.
