[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - Perturb(C) means C is set to 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - We need to determine which nodes are descendants of C in the graph.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   - C is a direct parent of A and D (C->A, C->D).
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - So, C's descendants are A and D.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - Therefore, perturbing C would set C to 0, and the nodes A and D would be 1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - Perturbing C: A:1, B:0, C:0, D:1
