[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m **Perturbation 2: Perturb(B)**  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - Perturb(B) means we set B to 0.  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - The downstream descendants of B are C and D (since B -> C and B -> D).  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - Therefore:  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   - B: 0 (perturbed),  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   - A: 1 (ancestor of B, not a descendant; but the question says "downstream descendant of the perturbed node." So A is not a descendant of B.  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   - C: 1 (descendant of B),  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   - D: 1 (descendant of B).  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - So the output should be: A:1, B:0, C:1, D:1.  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - But the given observation says: `Perturb(B) -> A:1 B:0 C:1 D:1`. ✅ This matches.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m **Perturbation 3: Perturb(C)**  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - Perturb(C) means we set C to 0.  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - The downstream descendants of C are none (no edges from C to other nodes).  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - Therefore:  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   - C: 0 (perturbed),  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   - A: 0 (not a descendant of C),  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   - B: 0 (not a descendant of C),  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   - D: 0 (not a descendant of C).  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - So the output should be: A:0, B:0, C:0, D:0.  
