[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m #### 2. Perturb(C)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - Perturb node C, so C is set to 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - Check which nodes are downstream descendants of C:  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   - C → D (so D is a downstream descendant)  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   - D → A (so A is a downstream descendant)  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   - Other nodes: B is not a downstream descendant of C.  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - Therefore, the effect should be:  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   A:1, B:0, C:0, D:1  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - The observed result is: A:1, B:0, C:0, D:1 → matches.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m #### 3. Perturb(D)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - Perturb node D, so D is set to 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m - Check which nodes are downstream descendants of D:  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=3563078)[0m   - D → A (so A is a downstream descendant)  
